{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@3c451eff-8e8f-49d9-b149-7ee0c380b058","sysml_id":"3c451eff-8e8f-49d9-b149-7ee0c380b058","element_id":"3c451eff-8e8f-49d9-b149-7ee0c380b058","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"87eda09d-2b91-44d7-b94a-f095b83200fb","owning_namespace_id":"87eda09d-2b91-44d7-b94a-f095b83200fb","owning_relationship_id":"23638814-75ee-46ed-a90d-4d8a7c5939d3","owning_membership_id":"23638814-75ee-46ed-a90d-4d8a7c5939d3","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"LWIR calibration, freshness, blockage and contrast estimates. Thermal-specific thresholds require validation; no perfect blockage observability is assumed. TDS_SEN_005, TDS_ODD_006. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@44d7f740-3834-4eff-9b9e-9e5fdc7a6e24","sysml_id":"44d7f740-3834-4eff-9b9e-9e5fdc7a6e24","element_id":"44d7f740-3834-4eff-9b9e-9e5fdc7a6e24","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"55c24ed9-4cae-4fe9-922a-65c7e5c682aa","owning_namespace_id":"55c24ed9-4cae-4fe9-922a-65c7e5c682aa","owning_relationship_id":"6b2efc57-e80b-4a2a-bba0-4a9c559e19b6","owning_membership_id":"6b2efc57-e80b-4a2a-bba0-4a9c559e19b6","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Activates the audible alarm within the allowed level range and\ndisplays the detected tiger bearing and distance.\nRequirements: TDS_WRN_001, TDS_WRN_002, TDS_WRN_003, TDS_WRN_005.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@492fd372-7250-42c8-a5b0-84a65da398f5","sysml_id":"492fd372-7250-42c8-a5b0-84a65da398f5","element_id":"492fd372-7250-42c8-a5b0-84a65da398f5","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"2cb72f32-dcf5-4973-acce-d6f215c8eba9","owning_namespace_id":"2cb72f32-dcf5-4973-acce-d6f215c8eba9","owning_relationship_id":"1806a61b-0fbb-4f7c-82ac-f0b6c10fae74","owning_membership_id":"1806a61b-0fbb-4f7c-82ac-f0b6c10fae74","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Monitored RGB + LWIR + lidar reference architecture. Sensor hardware\nsupplies measurements and available device diagnostics; channel-quality\nand blockage estimation are host software functions, not guaranteed\nembedded camera features. Fusion aligns data and produces unclassified\nhypotheses; ScanForTiger owns tiger classification. Requirement references identify the system contracts; SW requirements\ntrace to them through the RST satisfies attributes.\nPorts: one definition per payload, named after what it conveys and\ndeclaring its items as out. The sending side uses it as declared and the\nreceiving side conjugates it (~Name), which reverses every item it\ncarries. Both ends of a connection therefore share one port type, and a\npayload is declared once. A port usage carries no direction of its own;\nit is an input or an output because of the items its (possibly\nconjugated) definition declares, and the usage name records which.\nThis is a behavioral/interface specification, not executable perception\nsoftware or validated safety evidence. Healthy status does not establish\nSOTIF performance for every pose, target size, or thermal contrast.\n"},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@51a55f14-20ce-4789-b75a-58a8a5c18712","sysml_id":"51a55f14-20ce-4789-b75a-58a8a5c18712","element_id":"51a55f14-20ce-4789-b75a-58a8a5c18712","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"34a910d0-fd68-4365-bc28-8a5df14ab69c","owning_namespace_id":"34a910d0-fd68-4365-bc28-8a5df14ab69c","owning_relationship_id":"e2f10597-6ff5-4445-a0f2-e6cd50290be0","owning_membership_id":"e2f10597-6ff5-4445-a0f2-e6cd50290be0","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Performs tiger/non-tiger classification AFTER fusion and temporal confirmation, using both fused features and unclassified object hypotheses. It qualifies the result using current capability; a negative classification or healthy sensor status does not prove SOTIF coverage. Requirements: TDS_ALG_001 through TDS_ALG_004, TDS_SAF_003 through TDS_SAF_005. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
{"attributes":{"stable_path":"/documentation/Documentation@6355b952-b4fb-4119-85a2-39c3758cd01a","sysml_id":"6355b952-b4fb-4119-85a2-39c3758cd01a","element_id":"6355b952-b4fb-4119-85a2-39c3758cd01a","sysml_type":"Documentation","owner_id":"2477dc64-0b56-4cc6-b01a-9bbe8a70218c","owning_namespace_id":"2477dc64-0b56-4cc6-b01a-9bbe8a70218c","owning_relationship_id":"d6582bc2-e8bb-4f47-8459-9fa00443c26a","owning_membership_id":"d6582bc2-e8bb-4f47-8459-9fa00443c26a","is_library_element":false,"is_implied_included":false,"body":"Unclassified fused object hypotheses. Classifier ownership remains in ScanForTiger. "},"concept":"documentation","metamodel":"SysMLv2","namespace":"System_Model_Tiger_Detection"},
